// Alert query (DIAAT-205, new; DIAAT-285 rules): live dictation sessions whose Azure Speech
// sessions kept collapsing in the alert window. Replaces the browser Sentry alert on
// "speech.unhealthy" (the browser no longer reports to Sentry).
//
// Source (browser, OBS-4, dictation_speech_cancellations.kql; transcribe-web
// lib/dictation-session.ts, relayed by transcribe-api's POST /api/telemetry):
// "speech.unhealthy" - Speech sessions collapsing repeatedly (dictation.collapses_in_window
// in dictation.window_seconds); it fails the dictation session with "speech.unhealthy".
// Area: dictation only (DIAAT-205, decision 1). Relayed browser events carry no hmcts.area,
// so the area comes from the journey type's prefix ("dictation.session" -> "dictation").
// Every event of the "dictation.session" journey counts the session as active.
// Output: failures = distinct sessions with "speech.unhealthy" (hmcts.journey.id);
// failed_pct = 100 * failures / active sessions (context only). No code dimension on
// purpose: this alert counts collapsing sessions whatever the cause; the per-code view
// is alert_dictation_speech_failures.kql.
// Suggested rule (provisional, as the heritage thresholds): measure failures, Total,
// GreaterThanOrEqual 3 (as speech_failed_sessions), window PT30M, frequency PT10M,
// severity 2, no dimensions. Overlaps "speech-failures", which also counts this event
// per error code; this one pages on collapse even when the error codes are spread out.
customEvents
| where tostring(customDimensions["hmcts.journey.type"]) == "dictation.session"
| extend area = coalesce(tostring(customDimensions["hmcts.area"]),
    tostring(split(tostring(customDimensions["hmcts.journey.type"]), ".")[0]))
| where area == "dictation"
| extend journey_id = tostring(customDimensions["hmcts.journey.id"])
| summarize sessions = dcount(journey_id),
    failures = dcountif(journey_id, name == "speech.unhealthy")
| extend failed_pct = round(100.0 * failures / sessions, 1)
| project failures, failed_pct
